 "about_text": "Pace Gallery is a global contemporary art gallery founded in Boston in 1960 by Arne Glimcher, now led by CEO Marc Glimcher and President Samanthe Rubell. Working with roughly eighty artists and several estates, Pace's program pairs emerging and established contemporary figures with twentieth-century forebears, spanning painting, sculpture, photography, and light-based installation. The gallery operates spaces in New York, Los Angeles, London, Geneva, Berlin, Seoul, and Tokyo, with offices in Beijing and Hong Kong. Its Tokyo location, in the Azabudai Hills development, presents exhibitions by artists including Nigel Cooke and forms part of Pace's growing presence across Asia.",
